Room A
Room A.
You can see a tin plate, a lead plate, a brass key, an iron bell and an oak box (which is empty) here.
> spell red ball
R-E-D / B-A-L-L (2 vowels)
> spell oak b2x
O-A-K / B-#-X (2 vowels)
> hear tin bell tin
[again tin] Heard 3: tin bell tin. Oldest tin, newest tin.
> hear key zzz oak plate
[?] Heard 4: tin key oak plate. Oldest tin, newest plate.
> hear oak
[again oak] Heard 4: key oak plate oak. Oldest key, newest oak.
> echo red ball
[red ball] 8: LL4B DER.
A color.
> echo hello
[hello] 5: OLLEH.
Greeting.
> echo the iron bell
[the iron bell] 13, starts the, ends bell: LLEB NORI EHT.
3 letters, then more.
> echo quiet
[quiet] 5: TEIUQ.
Hush.
> echo zebra
[zebra] 5: 4RBEZ.
One word, 1 against m.
> echo abacus fab
[abacus fab] 10, ab at 0: B4F SUC4B4.
6 letters, then more.
> engrave tin plate with north gate
Cut into the tin plate.
> engrave tin plate with  bell
Cut into the tin plate.
> examine tin plate
The tin plate reads "north gate bell" (15 letters, 2 cuts).
> examine lead plate
The lead plate is blank.
> engrave key with x
That will not take a mark.
> label brass key
<BRASS KEY> depth 2/0, 11 chars.
> label lead plate
<LEAD PLATE> depth 2/0, 12 chars.
> trim iron bell
[--on bell] [on ] cmp -1, eq false.
> trim tin plate
[--n plate] [n p] cmp -1, eq true.
> shout brass key
THE BRASS KEY! / the brass key / 14 [the brass key] end
> shelve tin plate
1: tin plate.
> shelve brass key
2: brass key tin plate.
> shelve iron bell
3: brass key iron bell tin plate.
> shelve brass key
Already shelved.
